# Sources CI needs that are not released and so cannot be resolved by rosdep:
# the gz-maritime packages the vehicles load at run time. gz-sim loads their
# systems from GZ_SIM_SYSTEM_PLUGIN_PATH; nothing here links against them, but
# the tests spawn the vehicles in worlds that name them.
#
# * gz_thruster: gz-maritime-thruster-system, the thruster both vehicle
#   models name. It goes away when the normalized command mode reaches
#   gz-sim upstream and the models go back to gz-sim-thruster-system.
# * gz_hydrodynamics: gz-maritime-hydrodynamics-system, the damping both
#   vehicle models name, against the water rather than the ground.
# * gz_ocean_current: gz-maritime-ocean-current-system, the current the
#   vehicles' worlds own and gz_hydrodynamics reads.
# * gz_marked_shapes: a library gz_ocean_current builds on.
#
# Only those packages are copied into the workspace (see
# .github/workflows/ci.yml). Importing the whole repository would pull in
# gz_waves_provider_fft, whose ehukai dependency has no rosdep key either.
repositories:
  gz-maritime:
    type: git
    url: https://github.com/HonuRobotics/gz-maritime.git
    version: lyrical
